CORE gcc-only
main.c
--arch arm64 --unwind 3
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 19 restartable loop: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.unwind\.0\] line 23 unwinding assertion loop 0: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 32 counting loop: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line 33 one attempt: FAILURE$
^\[main\.unwind\.1\] line 38 unwinding assertion loop 1: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line 46 branch on success: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
approximating inline assembly
line 11 unwinding assertion
^\[main\.unwind\.2\]
--
The retry loop of a load-exclusive/store-exclusive sequence whose failed
attempts have no effect is replaced by the attempt that succeeds, so that it
needs no unwinding. Loops whose attempts are observable (here: counted), and
branches that are not taken just when the store fails, remain loops. The
assertions that fail may be violated on hardware, where a store-exclusive
may fail spuriously.
